SPEC='wiki/specs/update-helper-workflows.md';RESEARCH='wiki/research/update-helper-workflows.md'
def pages(data):
 packet='../../analysis/ableton-live-12.4.3/full-spec-v1/update-helper-workflows/'
 prefix='''This bounded analyst draft concerns externally named CLI, file and process roles in retained exact-build static evidence. It is not released implementation input or a runtime compatibility result. S means a role supported by selected retained static control flow; I means inference; U means unknown. Every target outcome remains U, every case is unexecuted, and every actual and documentary output/comparator is null. A source claim is prose provenance, not an oracle. No implementation algorithm, private identifier or pseudocode is prescribed here.\n\n'''
 spec='---\nid: SPEC-UPDATE-HELPER-WORKFLOWS\ntype: spec\nstatus: draft\nupdated: 2026-10-19\naccess: analysis\nrevision: 1\ntarget: Ableton Live 12 Suite 12.4.3; static retained arm64 roles only\n---\n\n# Update helper handoff workflows\n\n## Scope and authority\n\n'+prefix
 spec+='[Research](../research/update-helper-workflows.md) records evidence and limitations. [Delivery/recovery](delivery-recovery-workflows.md) retains public installation, authorization, update policy and recovery roles; existing project/media/ALS owners retain application-data validity. This packet adds only the selected prepared-handoff CLI/file/process predicates. Whole updater, account/network protocols, package preparation, OS authorization, platform parity and application compatibility remain outside this bounded contract.\n\n## Future evidence prerequisites\n\n'+data['cases'][0]['prerequisites']+' No operation is authorized by a case proposal. Audio consequences require their own independently nonzero active-path baseline and existing sound owners.\n\n## Requirements\n\n'
 for r in data['requirements']:
  spec+=f"### {r['id']} — {r['title']}\n\n**{r['provenance']}; target U.** {r['contract']}\n\nEvidence: "+(', '.join(r['evidence']) or 'none; explicit unknown')+'.\n\n'
 spec+='## Packet and limits\n\n[Requirement catalog]('+packet+'requirements.json), [cases]('+packet+'cases.json), [exact static locators]('+packet+'evidence.json), [source pins]('+packet+'source.json) and [read-only checker]('+packet+'validate.py) retain 30 requirements (21 S, 1 I, 8 U), 37 proposed cases and 22 evidence entries. All thirty requirements are semantically incomplete. Restoration attempts are not recovery guarantees; sentinel reachability does not prove successful marker creation; process names or source constants do not establish runtime matching or OS exit behavior.\n'
 research='---\nid: RESEARCH-UPDATE-HELPER-WORKFLOWS\ntype: research\nstatus: draft\nupdated: 2026-10-19\naccess: analysis\nrevision: 1\ntarget: Ableton Live 12 Suite 12.4.3\n---\n\n# Retained update helper evidence\n\n'+prefix
 research+='## Source availability and identity\n\nThe exact previously retained H6-WEB-V1 manifest, eight Swapper function bodies, selected connector/main/util bytecode listings and N4 Live-side startup/configuration excerpts are available. The current original helper fat file (20,820,496 bytes; SHA256 489a77c06a2ef1a770fa3cb7fc0f8f62d1ee20d57784aa0884d8dc58e1bd6c99), its recorded arm64 slice and three selected original bytecode files were hashed as data and match retained identities. No original code was imported, decoded, compiled or executed. No new source capture, runtime, tooling installation, process inspection, file replacement or updater operation occurred. The historical source date is 2026-10-17; exact UTC is unavailable and is null. Full original Live fat identity is inherited context, not newly verified.\n\n[Original source identity](sources/ableton-live-12.4.3.md), [H6 canonical analysis](web-addons-swapper-static.md) and [Live-side launch analysis](helper-launch-live-side.md) remain authoritative provenance context. Exact raw paths/hashes, historical manifests, parser origins and owner pins are in [source.json]('+packet+'source.json). All selected historical output hashes are reconciled, without rewriting their manifests.\n\n## Honest semantic read scope\n\nAll eight retained Swapper bodies (2,050 lines) were read, not merely their strings. The complete CLI declaration, parse/orchestration, replacement, rename-wrapper, marker, callback and entry contexts support the bounded roles. Most functions carry decompiler warnings; the rename wrapper is rendered void while callers consume a result. That type ambiguity is retained, not repaired into a new algorithm.\n\nSelected textual bytecode contexts were read for argument construction, configured-helper/apply admission, pending-ready flag, temporary executable relocation and invocation; the main install handoff retains originator completion, crash-marker and other-Live guards. The selected util process-check listing was read as static text. No claim covers the entire service, preparer, library-loader or process matching implementation. Selected N4 startup guard/callback/message/exit/name-provider, flag getters/setters and configuration excerpts plus callback reference/disassembly context were read. The large startup/configuration functions were not wholly reviewed; exact line ranges and JSON pointers in [evidence.json]('+packet+'evidence.json) delimit the claims.\n\n## Findings, inference and unresolved context\n\nThe supplied parent argument has a metadata/reporting role; it does not establish selection of the process awaited. Wait option wiring traverses a state constructor whose body is not in this bounded read, so REQ-UPDATE-HELPER-006 is I. The wait-forever label does not establish an endless loop or units for the retained constant. Path predicates do not establish precise filesystem validation or repair.\n\nSecond-promotion failure attempts restoration and reports failure even if restoration succeeds; restoration failure is a separate role. Cleanup failure follows promotion, reports failure and has no demonstrated restoration branch in the selected operation. Neither branch proves atomicity, durability, complete effects or successful rollback. Marker handling is reached only after reported operation success and nonempty supplied marker; ordinary marker error logging does not assign a fresh status in the selected routine. Exception closure and actual marker bytes/effects remain U.\n\nThe retained result constants include invalid invocation 2, detected Live 3, failed operation 1 and initial success 0; the selected Live startup guard exits through a retained 42 argument. These are research context only, never OS exit or runtime oracles. No timing units, diagnostic codec, ordering/flush or platform-wide status map is inferred. The selected Live route supplies configuration to a connector-launched helper, but does not establish absence of other launch/marker-reader routes.\n\n## Scoped questions\n\nQ-UH-001: CLI grammar/recovery and optional state constructor wiring. Q-UH-002: exact path predicate and rename-wrapper type ambiguity. Q-UH-003: wait/process identity, flag defaults and race policy. Q-UH-004: interrupted promotion/restoration/cleanup and durable recovery. Q-UH-005: marker/report codec, exceptions and OS status closure. Q-UH-006: selected Live guard/no-dialog admission and whole-callgraph closure. Q-UH-007: lifecycle/cancel/undo/source-loss/concurrency. Q-UH-008: platform, updater/account/network and data compatibility boundaries. These labels are scoped to this packet. Missing fixtures or capabilities remain U rather than passing negative cases.\n\n## Review and reproduction\n\n[Spec](../specs/update-helper-workflows.md), [case catalog]('+packet+'cases.json) and [counts]('+packet+'counts.json) are explicit partial draft material: 30 requirements, 37 future cases, zero executed, zero complete. The checker reads static data only and does not import original code or rewrite sealed outputs. Independent semantic review is pending.\n'
